Subject: [PATCH] rtl-sdr: drive FC0013 hardware AGC and periodic LNA control

The old-dab driver updates the FC0013 LNA from RSSI when tuner registers
are read. rtl_tcp performs this periodically, but the direct Welle input
did not. Run this control in the existing worker for automatic and manual
IF gain. Use tuner hardware AGC together with RTL2832 digital AGC for the
FC0013 automatic setting; leave other tuners on their existing gain path.

Serialize tuner control transfers against the periodic I2C access. Publish
amplitude measurements atomically and report input ring-buffer losses at
most once per five seconds, plus any remainder when reception stops.
This helps distinguish reception failure from decoder overload on MIPS.

References:
https://github.com/old-dab/rtlsdr/blob/64ff2ac8e9ecf35af28e1ccdf86d842037da3133/src/controlThread.c
https://github.com/old-dab/rtlsdr/blob/64ff2ac8e9ecf35af28e1ccdf86d842037da3133/src/tuner_fc001x.c
https://github.com/old-dab/rtlsdr/blob/64ff2ac8e9ecf35af28e1ccdf86d842037da3133/README_improvements.md

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [uses the old-dab RTL-SDR API selected by OpenATV]

